==Latin==

===Etymology===
The accusative singular masculine form of the pronominal stem {{m|la||na-}}; compare the interjection {{m|la|nē||truly”, “verily”, “really”, “indeed}}. Confer with its feminine form {{cog|la|nam}}, as in {{m|la|cum}}-{{m|la|quam}}, {{m|la|tum}}-{{m|la|tam}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/num/|lang=la}}

===Adverb===
{{head|la|adverbs}}

# [[now]] ''(only in the phrase, {{l|la|etiamnum|etiam num}})''
# (''in a direct question'') a particle expecting a [[negation]]
#: '''''Num''' Sparta insula est? — Non est insula.''
#:: What, is Sparta an island? — No, it's not.
# (''in an indirect question'') [[whether]]

